'''Somra''' (after its literary dialect), also known as '''Burmese Tangkhul''' (Tangkhul Naga), is a [[Sino-Tibetan languages|Sino-Tibetan]] language spoken in Myanmar. The two ethnic Tangkhul languages are related, but are not mutually intelligible, being only 30% lexically similar.<ref name=e18/> Somra is closer to [[Akyaung Ari language|Akyaung Ari]].

Somra is spoken in Somra tract, [[Leshi Township]] and [[Homalin Township]] of [[Sagaing Division]], Myanmar.

